# Original writer fixture: a recurring conversation hub with nested topics.
# Effects are requests to the host; this file never changes game state itself.
:: relay_desk default
> speaker=mara @desk_greeting
  If you're here about the transmitter, take a number. If you're here about the smoke, take a bucket.
? @ask_work
  Anything I can do to help?
  -> missing_courier
? @ask_station
  What happened to this place?
  -> station_history
? @insult_station
  Quite an operation. Does anything here actually work?
  -> insult
? @leave_desk
  I'll leave you to it.
  -> goodbye

:: missing_courier
> speaker=mara @courier_problem
  Our courier is two days late. Everyone keeps asking about the battery she was carrying. I'd rather know where she is.
? @ask_route
  Where was she headed?
  -> courier_route
? @offer_search
  I'll look for her.
  -> accept_search
? @back_from_work
  Let me ask about something else.
  -> relay_desk

:: courier_route
> speaker=mara @route_warning
  The old flood road. She knows it goes under at dusk, so don't tell me she simply got lost.
? @ask_shelter
  Is there somewhere she could shelter?
  -> pump_house
? @back_to_courier
  About the search...
  -> missing_courier

:: pump_house
> speaker=mara @shelter_hint
  A pump house, halfway out. Knock before you go in. She carries a flare pistol and she startles easily.
-> courier_route

:: accept_search
! immediate set_flag(courier_search, true)
! immediate change_disposition(mara, 1)
> speaker=mara @search_accepted
  Bring her home. The battery can walk back on its own, for all I care.
-> relay_desk

:: station_history
> speaker=mara @station_history_line
  We used to send weather reports. Now we send names. People listening for someone who hasn't come home.
? @ask_names
  Do you ever get an answer?
  -> station_answer
? @return_from_history
  Something else I wanted to ask.
  -> relay_desk

:: station_answer
> speaker=mara @answer_story
  Last week. A woman up north recognised her brother's cough before he said a word.
-> station_history

:: insult
! immediate change_disposition(mara, -1)
> speaker=mara @insult_response
  The door. Try it.
-> relay_desk

:: goodbye
> speaker=mara @farewell
  Keep off the flood road after dark.
-> END
